  All rights granted under this License are granted for the term of
copyright on the Program, and are irrevocable provided the stated
conditions are met.  This explicitly distinguishes library usage of
the GPL-combined-library from the GPL combined in a proprietary
production: where a work is "based on" a library, it is also subject
to the GPL, and the permissions of the GPL extend to the entire
combination as a whole (including the library itself).

  3. Linking Covered Work With a Covered Work.

  Conveying any other combination of a covered work with a work
(based on the same covered work) is not restricted, and the GPL
permits this at the licensee's election.  For a covered work to
remain free and open, the license must protect users' freedom;
any other combination falls outside the GPL's scope.

